 tri(1), ..., tri(n)]\n    return trib_sequence[0 : n + 1]", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}, {"task_id": "HumanEval/130", "solution": "def tri(n):\n    \"\"\"Everyone knows Fibonacci sequence, it was studied deeply by mathematicians in\n    the last couple centuries. However, what people don't know is Tribonacci sequence.\n    Tribonacci sequence is defined by the recurrence:\n    tri(1) = 3\n    tri(n) = 1 + n / 2, if n is even.\n    tri(n) =  tri(n - 1) + tri(n - 2) + tri(n + 1), if n is odd.\n    For example:\n    tri(2) = 1 + (2 / 2) = 2\n    tri(4) = 3\n    tri(3) = tri(2) + tri(1) + tri(4)\n           = 2 + 3 + 3 = 8\n    You are given a non-negative integer number n, you have to a return a list of the\n    first n + 1 numbers of the Tribonacci sequence.\n    Examples:\n    tri(3) = [1, 3, 2, 8]\n    \"\"\"\n\n    _memo = {}\n\n    def _calculate_term(k):\n        if k in _memo:\n            return _memo[k]\n\n        if k == 0:\n            result = 1\n        elif k == 1:\n            result = 3\n        elif k % 2 == 0:  # k is even and k >= 2\n            result = 1 + k // 2  # Use integer division\n        else:  # k is odd and k >= 3\n            # These recursive calls will populate _memo as needed\n            val_k_minus_1 = _calculate_term(k - 1)\n            val_k_minus_2 = _calculate_term(k - 2)\n            val_k_plus_1 = _calculate_term(k + 1)\n            result = val_k_minus_1 + val_k_minus_2 + val_k_plus_1\n\n        _memo[k] = result\n        return result\n\n    sequence = []\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        sequence.append(_calculate_term(i))\n\n    return sequence", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "HumanEval/148": [{"task_id": "HumanEval/148", "solution": "class Planet:\n    \"\"\"Represents a planet with its name and orbital order.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, name: str, orbit_order: int):\n        self.name = na